WEBVTT

1
00:01:25.541 --> 00:01:26.708
You never know people.

2
00:01:26.791 --> 00:01:30.166
The people closest to you will
surprise you the most.

3
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.166
I thought it'd be impossible
to explain the concept

4
00:01:33.291 --> 00:01:34.833
of a "situationship" to my dad.

5
00:01:34.916 --> 00:01:36.666
I told him that basically,

6
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.166
you hook up with each other, eat together,

7
00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.833
Netflix and chill and that's it.

8
00:01:41.666 --> 00:01:45.208
You don't share your emotions
or real feelings.

9
00:01:45.291 --> 00:01:46.333
And my dad was like,

10
00:01:46.416 --> 00:01:48.833
"Son, I have done all that
with your mother."

11
00:01:48.916 --> 00:01:50.333
"It's called arranged marriage."

12
00:01:51.791 --> 00:01:52.875
I was like, okay!

13
00:01:55.166 --> 00:01:56.291
You never know people.

14
00:01:56.375 --> 00:01:57.583
I have a childhood friend.

15
00:01:58.291 --> 00:02:01.583
We were at boarding school together.
We shared dreams.

16
00:02:01.708 --> 00:02:04.083
And today, guys, he's sitting
in the audience with you.

17
00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:05.791
And since I've been on the stage,

18
00:02:06.375 --> 00:02:07.625
he's been on his phone.

19
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.125
Bro, you had one fucking job!

20
00:02:11.208 --> 00:02:13.333
Sit here and laugh loudly,

21
00:02:13.416 --> 00:02:15.500
so that I'd win this open mic.

22
00:02:15.583 --> 00:02:16.583
Go, Imaad!

23
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:20.708
By the way, Neil is neither
in a relationship or situationship.

24
00:02:20.791 --> 00:02:22.166
And I wonder why.

25
00:02:22.666 --> 00:02:24.375
I mean, he's a gym trainer.

26
00:02:24.458 --> 00:02:27.666
5'5'' tall. He lives with his parents.

27
00:02:28.375 --> 00:02:29.750
What could be wrong?

28
00:02:34.541 --> 00:02:37.291
There's my other childhood friend.

29
00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:40.416
Ahana. She's also my flatmate.

30
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.416
We aren't in a situation-ship.
We're in a space-ship.

31
00:02:45.625 --> 00:02:47.750
We give each other a lot of space.

32
00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:49.583
She stays in her room, I in mine.

33
00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:51.708
I have my girlfriends and she has Rohan.

34
00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.375
Look at them, guys.
They're so adorable, so cute!

35
00:02:56.458 --> 00:02:57.500
Stop.

36
00:02:57.583 --> 00:02:59.458
They've been dating for two years.

37
00:02:59.541 --> 00:03:00.375
Three!

38
00:03:00.458 --> 00:03:04.208
Three years. I'm worried
they'll soon get married.

39
00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.166
But you know, Ahana,

40
00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:08.916
I'm not ready for you
to leave this space-ship.

41
00:03:09.666 --> 00:03:13.000
So, Rohan, tell you what.
Move in with us after marriage.

42
00:03:13.083 --> 00:03:14.791
-Yeah.
-Done!

43
00:03:14.875 --> 00:03:17.083
And, guys, I hear Rohan cooks very well.

44
00:03:17.166 --> 00:03:18.208
He's well-organized.

45
00:03:18.291 --> 00:03:20.500
And it's time
we get a full-time house help.

46
00:03:21.625 --> 00:03:22.625
Shut up, Imaad!

47
00:03:22.708 --> 00:03:25.166
Jokes apart, we'll call him Junior.

48
00:03:26.208 --> 00:03:29.166
And it has nothing to do with the pictures
you sent Ahana last night.

49
00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.333
Imaad!

50
00:03:39.083 --> 00:03:44.541
All we've got to say is this

51
00:03:47.041 --> 00:03:52.875
We'll live the way we want to live

52
00:03:55.458 --> 00:03:57.583
There's nothing

53
00:03:57.666 --> 00:04:00.083
that can bring us down

54
00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:08.750
We'll take the path our hearts have found

55
00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:13.833
People go, people stay

56
00:04:13.916 --> 00:04:18.166
Let it happen anyway

57
00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:22.083
These days are new and nights are young

58
00:04:22.166 --> 00:04:27.166
Let new songs be sung

59
00:04:30.416 --> 00:04:32.833
Let it happen anyway

60
00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:39.875
We have all the happiness we'll ever need

61
00:04:42.208 --> 00:04:47.666
We're masters of our destiny

62
00:04:51.125 --> 00:04:53.875
What can stop us now?

63
00:04:53.958 --> 00:04:58.208
People go, people stay

64
00:04:58.291 --> 00:05:02.083
Let it happen anyway

65
00:05:02.166 --> 00:05:06.208
These days are new and nights are young

66
00:05:06.291 --> 00:05:11.208
Let new songs be sung

67
00:05:11.291 --> 00:05:14.250
If you feel

68
00:05:14.916 --> 00:05:19.333
Your lover drift away

69
00:05:19.416 --> 00:05:23.041
Just follow

70
00:05:23.125 --> 00:05:26.958
What your heart will say

71
00:05:27.041 --> 00:05:30.875
People go, people stay

72
00:05:30.958 --> 00:05:34.625
Let it happen anyway

73
00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:39.291
These days are new and nights are young

74
00:05:39.375 --> 00:05:43.041
Let new tales be told, new songs be sung

75
00:05:43.125 --> 00:05:50.083
People go, people stay
Let it happen anyway

76
00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:53.083
These days are new and nights are young

77
00:05:53.166 --> 00:05:55.333
Happy New Year!

78
00:05:55.416 --> 00:06:01.000
Let new tales be told, new songs be sung

79
00:06:53.333 --> 00:06:54.666
Good morning.

80
00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:57.625
Hey, you've left?
Why didn't you wake me up?

81
00:06:58.291 --> 00:07:00.958
You looked so peaceful.
I didn't have the heart.

82
00:07:01.625 --> 00:07:04.291
How sweet! Call me later?

83
00:07:05.083 --> 00:07:06.708
Sure. Bye.

84
00:07:06.791 --> 00:07:07.791
See you.

85
00:07:16.333 --> 00:07:18.541
I need to be on my own for some time.

86
00:07:18.625 --> 00:07:22.208
-Tell me the truth.
-There's no one else.

87
00:07:22.291 --> 00:07:24.125
Then what happened? I don't understand!

88
00:07:24.208 --> 00:07:26.791
Ahana, I told you,
I need some clarity in my life.

89
00:07:26.916 --> 00:07:29.250
-I don't know what I'm doing.
-What are you doing?

90
00:07:31.458 --> 00:07:33.666
I must focus on my career.

91
00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:36.375
I need some space. That's all.

92
00:07:36.875 --> 00:07:39.833
Are you an astronaut?
Need space for your career?

93
00:07:40.625 --> 00:07:42.791
You work in your dad's firm.

94
00:07:43.666 --> 00:07:45.958
Please, Rohan, I know
you wanna hook up with other girls.

95
00:07:48.416 --> 00:07:50.250
I just-- I'm done. I can't…

96
00:07:50.333 --> 00:07:52.458
-Can't do what? What, Rohan?
-I just can't.

97
00:07:52.541 --> 00:07:53.875
-Huh?
-Nothing.

98
00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.833
Nothing ever happens.
Maybe that's the problem!

99
00:07:58.416 --> 00:08:00.625
Is this about sex? We can work on it.

100
00:08:00.708 --> 00:08:02.125
That's another story.

101
00:08:02.208 --> 00:08:04.333
I spoke about marriage.
It freaked you out.

102
00:08:04.416 --> 00:08:06.166
-There's no rush.
-I'm not freaking out.

103
00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.291
I just need a break.

104
00:08:11.625 --> 00:08:13.541
For how long? A month? Three months?

105
00:08:13.625 --> 00:08:14.833
I don't know!

106
00:08:16.333 --> 00:08:18.166
What do I tell my parents?

107
00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:20.208
-I don't know.
-What do you know?

108
00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.583
Is the house on fire?

109
00:08:47.666 --> 00:08:48.666
What?

110
00:08:49.208 --> 00:08:51.708
-Why was Rohan rushing out?
-Shut up!

111
00:08:59.125 --> 00:09:00.625
What's happened now?

112
00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.541
He wants a break.

113
00:09:08.291 --> 00:09:10.333
-From when?
-From now.

114
00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.625
Don't worry, he'll be back.

115
00:09:22.333 --> 00:09:24.958
And if he doesn't,
there's always arranged marriage.

116
00:09:27.916 --> 00:09:29.041
How was your date?

117
00:09:29.625 --> 00:09:31.208
Cute. Journalist.

118
00:09:31.291 --> 00:09:34.000
Cute? Seeing her again?

119
00:09:37.041 --> 00:09:38.625
You've got issues, bro.

120
00:09:39.875 --> 00:09:41.666
Don't tell Neil.

121
00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:45.333
He doesn't like Rohan.
When we get back, it'll be awkward.

122
00:09:45.416 --> 00:09:46.625
Okay.

123
00:09:51.833 --> 00:09:52.958
Morning, Neil.

124
00:09:53.041 --> 00:09:55.333
-Baby, your breakfast is ready.
-Thanks, Mama.

125
00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:57.875
And your parcel came yesterday.

126
00:09:58.875 --> 00:09:59.833
Thank you.

127
00:10:02.958 --> 00:10:04.958
-How was Mass?
-It was fine.

128
00:10:07.833 --> 00:10:08.750
Protein got over?

129
00:10:09.291 --> 00:10:10.708
Didn't you just order some?

130
00:10:11.625 --> 00:10:12.791
Neil, 8,000?

131
00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:17.250
-Who asked you to check the bill?
-Someone has to.

132
00:10:17.916 --> 00:10:22.041
Every day 12 egg whites, salmon.
Isn't that enough protein for you?

133
00:10:22.166 --> 00:10:25.250
So I paid for it. I can pay
for everything else too if you want.

134
00:10:25.333 --> 00:10:27.458
Can we please have our breakfast in peace?

135
00:10:27.583 --> 00:10:29.791
All I want is for you to save your money.

136
00:10:29.875 --> 00:10:32.000
And 20 pairs of shoes? Why do you have it?

137
00:10:32.083 --> 00:10:33.791
I need proper sneakers.

138
00:10:34.291 --> 00:10:37.416
Your generation doesn't know
the difference between need and want.

139
00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.583
T-shirts and shorts!

140
00:10:38.708 --> 00:10:41.250
Only I know how hard I work
to run this house.

141
00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:52.083
"I don't know
what I've done to upset you."

142
00:10:52.916 --> 00:10:54.625
"Have I done anything at all?"

143
00:10:54.708 --> 00:10:57.958
"This isn't the first time we've argued,
or the last."

144
00:10:58.916 --> 00:11:01.708
"So can you please just tell me
why you want a break?"

145
00:11:02.291 --> 00:11:06.000
"Just don't say you're bored of me.
Or you're looking for someone new."

146
00:11:07.375 --> 00:11:09.291
"I don't understand what you want."

147
00:11:09.791 --> 00:11:11.416
"What are you looking for?"

148
00:11:12.458 --> 00:11:14.166
"What we have is precious, Rohan."

149
00:11:14.875 --> 00:11:17.500
"I don't know
when we stopped communicating."

150
00:11:18.541 --> 00:11:21.083
"Please call me. I'll be waiting."

151
00:11:25.833 --> 00:11:30.833
Hold my hand because I'm taking you
with me to Lalaland.

152
00:11:30.916 --> 00:11:33.333
I'm Lala, but of course you know that.

153
00:11:33.416 --> 00:11:38.958
And today I've brought you all
to sunny, gorgeous Maldives!

154
00:11:39.041 --> 00:11:41.125
To celebrate you guys!

155
00:11:41.208 --> 00:11:43.500
All one million of you.

156
00:11:43.583 --> 00:11:45.791
So let's dance, shake a hip.

157
00:11:45.875 --> 00:11:47.916
Run on the sand, take a dip in the pool.

158
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:51.125
'Cause life is la-la-la!

159
00:11:51.208 --> 00:11:54.333
At the beautiful Maldives sea villa.

160
00:11:54.916 --> 00:11:57.708
Why does she deserve a free vacation?

161
00:11:58.291 --> 00:11:59.791
She has a million followers, bro.

162
00:11:59.875 --> 00:12:02.541
Wear a bikini and the boys will follow.

163
00:12:02.625 --> 00:12:03.875
Just shut up, man.

164
00:12:04.666 --> 00:12:06.000
She's an influencer.

165
00:12:06.083 --> 00:12:08.875
Who's influenced
by this inflatable horsey?

166
00:12:08.958 --> 00:12:11.875
It works, dude.
People don't know it's all sponsored.

167
00:12:11.958 --> 00:12:14.416
-Hotels, trips, right?
-Exactly.

168
00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.125
-She's a marketing genius.
-What?

169
00:12:16.208 --> 00:12:19.708
Looks like the next Neil Pereira rom-com
is coming in a theatre near you.

170
00:12:19.791 --> 00:12:22.375
C'mon, guys, grow up. She's my client.

171
00:12:22.458 --> 00:12:25.291
Client? You went to the Maldives with her?

172
00:12:25.375 --> 00:12:26.458
Yeah, so?

173
00:12:26.541 --> 00:12:27.541
To carry her bags?

174
00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:29.708
To train her.

175
00:12:29.791 --> 00:12:30.875
-To train her!
-Train her.

176
00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:34.541
-Why didn't you post any selfies with her?
-She's just a client, yeah?

177
00:12:35.125 --> 00:12:37.375
Do I need to post every minute of my life?

178
00:12:37.458 --> 00:12:39.833
-This is a little shady.
-Very shady.

179
00:12:41.583 --> 00:12:42.416
Okay, fine.

180
00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.625
-Fine? What's that?
-Fine?

181
00:12:44.708 --> 00:12:46.541
-Fine.
-Fine what?

182
00:12:46.625 --> 00:12:48.166
Fine what?

183
00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:50.291
-It's more than that.
-I knew it!

184
00:12:50.375 --> 00:12:51.208
Since when?

185
00:12:51.833 --> 00:12:53.083
It's been a few months.

186
00:12:53.791 --> 00:12:55.458
You've hid it for months?

187
00:12:56.416 --> 00:12:59.125
-She doesn't want people to know.
-So are we just "people"?

188
00:12:59.208 --> 00:13:03.333
Bro, her followers must think
she's single. Attainable.

189
00:13:03.916 --> 00:13:06.875
-We're not her followers.
-You're still not?

190
00:13:06.958 --> 00:13:08.458
-No!
-We're your friends.

191
00:13:09.083 --> 00:13:12.625
So behave like friends.
Just give me some privacy.

192
00:13:12.708 --> 00:13:14.250
-Imaad, he wants privacy.
-Privacy.

193
00:13:14.375 --> 00:13:16.833
-We'll give him privacy.
-You piece of shit!

194
00:13:16.958 --> 00:13:18.958
You want privacy?
When are we gonna meet her?

195
00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:21.791
You want privacy, do you?

196
00:13:27.875 --> 00:13:29.000
Sorry.

197
00:13:31.041 --> 00:13:33.916
Seriously, bro,
this AI shit could end careers.

198
00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.208
Yours maybe. Mine hasn't started.

199
00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.666
It'll happen, man. You'll be fine.

200
00:13:40.166 --> 00:13:41.791
You're the man. You're good.

201
00:13:42.666 --> 00:13:44.041
Good doesn't cut it anymore, bro.

202
00:13:44.125 --> 00:13:47.500
These days you need to have your
own brand and celebrity clients.

203
00:13:47.583 --> 00:13:49.291
So? You have a celeb. Lala.

204
00:13:49.916 --> 00:13:53.208
Lala today, Lolo tomorrow,
then Bebo. Then Saifu!

205
00:13:58.666 --> 00:14:01.833
But seriously, man, I don't know
what the fuck I'm doing with my life.

206
00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:07.208
I want to open my own gym.
That'll be a game changer.

207
00:14:07.291 --> 00:14:08.250
So do it!

208
00:14:09.291 --> 00:14:11.125
You should've told me earlier.

209
00:14:11.208 --> 00:14:14.291
I have some rupees saved. I can open
two branches this week. What say?

210
00:14:16.375 --> 00:14:19.125
Man, I have no idea what I'm doing either.

211
00:14:19.208 --> 00:14:21.916
Tell you what.
Let's try till we're thirty.

212
00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:25.458
And if nothing works out,
Ahana will support us both.

213
00:14:25.541 --> 00:14:27.625
I'm sure she's already planning for it.

214
00:14:28.208 --> 00:14:29.958
Ahana's sorted, man.

215
00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:32.750
What is she doing with Rohan?

216
00:14:34.625 --> 00:14:35.833
Rohan wants a break.

217
00:14:36.416 --> 00:14:39.083
-What?
-I didn't say a word. You know nothing.

218
00:14:40.958 --> 00:14:42.833
Rohan wants a break from Ahana?

219
00:14:44.583 --> 00:14:46.458
-Guts.
-I know.

220
00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:48.208
Guts.

221
00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:50.833
-Bottoms up!
-Bottoms up!

222
00:15:12.666 --> 00:15:14.750
PLEASE CALL ME. I'M WAITING.

223
00:15:36.833 --> 00:15:39.375
Why has Rohan posted
a photo of a cake at dawn?

224
00:15:39.958 --> 00:15:40.958
What?

225
00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.708
-Bro, that's a cupcake.
-Same thing.

226
00:15:43.791 --> 00:15:45.416
How's it the same thing?

227
00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.750
-A cupcake is part of the cake family.
-So?

228
00:15:47.833 --> 00:15:50.000
A cupcake has its own identity.

229
00:15:50.083 --> 00:15:52.791
Its own personality.
You'd call a pastry a cake?

230
00:15:52.875 --> 00:15:54.333
-You nuts?
-A pastry is a pastry.

231
00:15:54.416 --> 00:15:55.375
-You're mad.
-You are.

232
00:15:55.458 --> 00:15:57.916
If I post a photo of an Alsatian,
I can't call it a dog?

233
00:15:58.041 --> 00:16:00.083
-South Bombay elitist!
-You call Messi by name.

234
00:16:00.166 --> 00:16:01.875
-Navi Mumbai is…
-Your dad's house…

235
00:16:01.958 --> 00:16:03.750
Shut up! Just shut up!

236
00:16:12.916 --> 00:16:15.916
I want a break, or I want to break up?

237
00:16:16.958 --> 00:16:19.916
Ahana, is the Adrena-Fit
proposal deck ready?

238
00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:22.708
-I've mailed it to you.
-Great. Thank you.

239
00:16:23.583 --> 00:16:26.708
You planned the whole strategy
and she'll take the credit.

240
00:16:28.291 --> 00:16:30.583
He uploaded a photo of a cake
this morning.

241
00:16:30.666 --> 00:16:33.875
-What?
-Yeah, cupcake. And a heart.

242
00:16:33.958 --> 00:16:35.208
Cupcake?

243
00:16:37.166 --> 00:16:38.250
Let's check.

244
00:16:39.375 --> 00:16:45.125
Stacy Gomes, Mrinalini Jaisinghani,
Trisha Mariwala, Anoushka Gupta.

245
00:16:45.708 --> 00:16:47.333
-Kylie Jenner…
-Kylie Jenner.

246
00:16:47.416 --> 00:16:49.291
Dude, all boys follow Kylie.

247
00:16:49.375 --> 00:16:52.083
-Who's the dream girl?
-Ayush's sister.

248
00:16:52.166 --> 00:16:55.041
-Butter Cupcakes?
-Open that.

249
00:16:57.666 --> 00:16:59.750
This is where the cupcake was from.

250
00:17:02.333 --> 00:17:03.958
"Tanyabuttercupfly."

251
00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:06.125
Tanya Mehra.

252
00:17:06.208 --> 00:17:10.250
Just a girl with a sweet tooth
and a sweet life. Sparkle emoji.

253
00:17:11.458 --> 00:17:13.666
Always remember to sprinkle laughter,

254
00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:17.291
spontaneity and kindness
onto every single cupcake.

255
00:17:17.375 --> 00:17:20.041
#baketheworldabetterplace.

256
00:17:22.375 --> 00:17:23.458
Let me see.

257
00:17:30.583 --> 00:17:34.125
-Let's check her stories.
-She'll see my name.

258
00:17:34.625 --> 00:17:37.250
We'll make a fake account. Give.

259
00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:44.458
"I want a break" basically means,
"I want to hook up with someone else."

260
00:17:45.166 --> 00:17:48.458
You said you were never in a relationship.

261
00:17:48.541 --> 00:17:50.208
-Then how so sure?
-I know, right?

262
00:17:50.291 --> 00:17:51.875
Maybe I should be a therapist.

263
00:17:52.416 --> 00:17:55.125
But I can't pull off your cardigan look.

264
00:17:56.666 --> 00:17:59.500
You come to this session
to talk about you.

265
00:18:00.125 --> 00:18:02.333
Not about Ahana or my cardigan.

266
00:18:02.416 --> 00:18:03.750
Aren't we stuck in a loop?

267
00:18:04.333 --> 00:18:07.208
I think you've built a wall
around yourself.

268
00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:11.083
And you won't let anyone in.

269
00:18:12.541 --> 00:18:14.833
But you deserve a healthy,
loving relationship.

270
00:18:15.541 --> 00:18:19.000
What I really deserve is for dad
to stop sending me to these sessions.

271
00:18:21.583 --> 00:18:24.000
You know, Imaad, the thing about shame is

272
00:18:24.541 --> 00:18:28.875
the more you hide it, the more it grows.

273
00:18:30.291 --> 00:18:33.916
-But when we've talked about it--
-It's been 14 years.

274
00:18:35.166 --> 00:18:36.750
Let's both forget it.

275
00:18:41.083 --> 00:18:42.750
Where did you buy your cardigan?

276
00:18:44.125 --> 00:18:46.291
-You're sure this will work?
-Trust me, bro.

277
00:18:47.083 --> 00:18:49.958
It'll strengthen the glutes,
build endurance,

278
00:18:50.041 --> 00:18:52.583
-and it'll also protect the knees.
-That's good.

279
00:18:52.666 --> 00:18:54.916
That's it. Squat, hold that, stabilize.

280
00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.000
Pelvis tucked in. Chest up, bam!

281
00:18:57.083 --> 00:18:59.875
-Shoulders drop, yeah.
-Perfect.

282
00:18:59.958 --> 00:19:02.791
-Let's go for one last. Just on one leg.
-All right.

283
00:19:02.875 --> 00:19:04.708
This will strengthen your glutes.

284
00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:08.208
-It'll build endurance.
-One, two.

285
00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:09.666
One more.

286
00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.416
Protect the knees from injury.
Drop your shoulders.

287
00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:13.833
Lengthen the spine.

288
00:19:14.708 --> 00:19:16.500
Breathe. Smile.

289
00:19:19.625 --> 00:19:23.708
-Why can't I look like Malaika?
-Why do you need to?

290
00:19:23.791 --> 00:19:26.500
Take care of yourself
and that makes you beautiful, right?

291
00:19:27.125 --> 00:19:29.791
C'mon, nine, ten.

292
00:19:30.375 --> 00:19:31.625
C'mon, Anita, let's go.

293
00:19:32.958 --> 00:19:33.833
Eleven.

294
00:19:34.666 --> 00:19:36.750
I might not know Uganda's capital,

295
00:19:36.833 --> 00:19:40.166
but I know what Malaika Arora wore
to the gym yesterday.

296
00:19:41.708 --> 00:19:43.958
Even our attention span is
getting shorter.

297
00:19:44.041 --> 00:19:46.000
We used to watch five-day test matches.

298
00:19:46.083 --> 00:19:49.208
And now if a video isn't interesting
in the first five seconds,

299
00:19:49.291 --> 00:19:50.708
we go, "This guy is a drag!"

300
00:19:51.625 --> 00:19:54.833
I think the only people
who can perform in less than five seconds

301
00:19:54.958 --> 00:19:56.250
are Indian men in bed.

302
00:20:00.291 --> 00:20:01.791
Too close to home, ma'am!

303
00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:04.708
Are you guys together?

304
00:20:04.791 --> 00:20:05.750
Sorry, sir.

305
00:20:08.958 --> 00:20:12.333
We come across someone's profile
who has a life we aspire to have,

306
00:20:12.416 --> 00:20:14.625
we instantly follow them.

307
00:20:16.083 --> 00:20:19.166
We feel insecure and depressed
looking at the profile,

308
00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:20.958
but we are willingly following it.

309
00:20:21.041 --> 00:20:22.541
How stupid is that?

310
00:20:23.291 --> 00:20:26.291
If you want a daily reminder
that you're a disappointment,

311
00:20:26.458 --> 00:20:27.458
just call your dad.

312
00:20:27.541 --> 00:20:30.458
He's still wishing his son will
change the world one day.

313
00:20:32.083 --> 00:20:37.875
I read a survey that an average person
checks their phone 224 times a day. Wow!

314
00:20:37.958 --> 00:20:41.250
If you're repeating an activity
224 times a day,

315
00:20:41.333 --> 00:20:43.541
it's not an activity, it's an addiction.

316
00:20:45.541 --> 00:20:48.833
And we have become addicted
to other peoples' lives.

317
00:20:48.916 --> 00:20:52.708
Enough! We've got blinders on
and our brains in a straitjacket.

318
00:20:53.916 --> 00:20:56.833
I don't want to know what you're doing,
thinking or eating.

319
00:20:56.958 --> 00:20:58.250
I have better things to do.

320
00:20:58.333 --> 00:21:01.375
Like finding out what Malaika Arora
wore to the gym today.

321
00:21:03.458 --> 00:21:05.291
That's my time, thank you so much.

322
00:21:05.375 --> 00:21:09.458
Also, we have a very special guest
tonight, and a dear friend.

323
00:21:09.541 --> 00:21:11.708
Please give it up for Sapan Verma!

324
00:21:16.708 --> 00:21:20.208
Hello! Give it up for Imaad, everybody.
C'mon, once more!

325
00:21:20.291 --> 00:21:22.875
We need some commercial material.

326
00:21:22.958 --> 00:21:25.000
Something meme-worthy that goes viral.

327
00:21:25.083 --> 00:21:28.916
Tap into tier two, tier three space, man.
Take it to the next level.

328
00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:31.458
That's my next level?
Become a meme or a virus?

329
00:21:31.541 --> 00:21:34.125
Of course! Anyway, listen to me.

330
00:21:34.208 --> 00:21:36.375
There's a high-profile wedding next week.

331
00:21:36.458 --> 00:21:38.583
-You're hosting it.
-And you're gonna dance.

332
00:21:40.291 --> 00:21:42.666
-Bye, Melbun.
-That means we're on, right?

333
00:21:43.666 --> 00:21:46.666
-Did you see the new Vir Das special?
-Yes.

334
00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:47.750
It was okay.

335
00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:50.500
Okay?

336
00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:55.333
I loved it.
The way he worked the audience.

337
00:21:55.416 --> 00:21:56.583
When's your special?

338
00:21:57.500 --> 00:22:00.250
-It'll happen. Takes time.
-Set a cutoff date.

339
00:22:00.333 --> 00:22:01.916
When I was your age, I was a self--

340
00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:04.416
I know! You had your own car and kids.

341
00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:06.250
Even walked on the moon.

342
00:22:07.375 --> 00:22:09.583
I can look after myself, Dad. Don't worry.

343
00:22:09.666 --> 00:22:10.541
I know.

344
00:22:11.125 --> 00:22:13.375
All I'm saying is, be smart.

345
00:22:13.458 --> 00:22:16.958
The house and money your mother
left you won't last forever.

346
00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:19.083
-Hmm?
-Hmm.

347
00:22:21.583 --> 00:22:22.750
Imaad bhaiya!

348
00:22:22.833 --> 00:22:24.000
Hey!

349
00:22:24.083 --> 00:22:27.000
-Hello!
-Hello! Hi!

350
00:22:27.833 --> 00:22:29.500
-Bedtime?
-Yes.

351
00:22:30.125 --> 00:22:32.750
-Give your brother a kiss. Come on.
-Come on.

352
00:22:36.125 --> 00:22:37.458
Drive the knee up.

353
00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:42.916
Close. That's it. Good. Come down.

354
00:22:44.333 --> 00:22:47.958
Yeah, and all the way up,
and maintain that line.

355
00:22:48.791 --> 00:22:49.875
Kettlebell close.

356
00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:53.000
Engage the core. C'mon, Lala, focus!

357
00:22:53.958 --> 00:22:56.000
-Man!
-What's up?

358
00:22:56.666 --> 00:22:59.125
That old man keeps staring
through that window.

359
00:22:59.208 --> 00:23:01.000
-What old man?
-Nothing.

360
00:23:02.208 --> 00:23:04.916
Don't open it.
He just stands right there and stares.

361
00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:06.500
File a complaint.

362
00:23:07.208 --> 00:23:09.208
