-That he keeps staring.

363
00:23:10.458 --> 00:23:12.250
Half the country would be in jail then.

364
00:23:12.958 --> 00:23:14.166
Unbelievable!

365
00:23:16.041 --> 00:23:17.041
You're cute.

366
00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:19.166
Finish your set, c'mon.

367
00:23:24.916 --> 00:23:26.916
And very professional.

368
00:23:40.583 --> 00:23:42.541
Ahana and Imaad want to meet you.

369
00:23:44.375 --> 00:23:45.791
What's your scene tomorrow?

370
00:23:46.708 --> 00:23:49.458
I'm taking my parents out
for dinner tomorrow.

371
00:23:51.166 --> 00:23:52.375
Some other time?

372
00:23:53.083 --> 00:23:54.416
Yeah, sounds good.

373
00:23:56.208 --> 00:23:59.750
Come, let's get some squats in.
Come on. Let's go!

374
00:24:05.791 --> 00:24:06.666
Zeeshan?

375
00:24:07.250 --> 00:24:08.625
-Hi, Simran.
-Hi.

376
00:24:13.833 --> 00:24:15.375
-Please come in.
-Thanks.

377
00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:18.916
Oh, wow!

378
00:24:23.250 --> 00:24:27.041
-You know, I wasn't expecting this.
-Is that a compliment or an insult?

379
00:24:27.125 --> 00:24:29.833
No, no, it's really nice.
It's got character.

380
00:24:30.500 --> 00:24:34.625
Some things look brand new, others look
like they've been here forever.

381
00:24:40.500 --> 00:24:43.208
So I think we should just
jump right into it.

382
00:24:43.291 --> 00:24:47.125
Might be a bit awkward at first,
but, you know…

383
00:24:47.208 --> 00:24:50.291
I usually don't allow a camera
on the first date.

384
00:24:51.375 --> 00:24:53.541
I told you I wanted to photograph you.

385
00:24:54.333 --> 00:24:56.125
I thought that was an excuse.

386
00:24:56.208 --> 00:24:58.083
No, I'm a photographer.

387
00:24:58.166 --> 00:25:00.958
It's for a project of mine.
It's called "The people of Tinder."

388
00:25:01.583 --> 00:25:03.875
Nice. So you want to interview me?

389
00:25:03.958 --> 00:25:04.916
Kinda.

390
00:25:06.083 --> 00:25:07.083
Con artist.

391
00:25:08.083 --> 00:25:08.916
That's me.

392
00:25:12.208 --> 00:25:15.791
So you want to meet the person
behind the profile?

393
00:25:15.875 --> 00:25:18.125
Thanks. I guess.

394
00:25:18.208 --> 00:25:22.041
I want to understand
who you are when you're alone.

395
00:25:22.125 --> 00:25:23.500
But I'm not alone.

396
00:25:24.083 --> 00:25:26.500
Yeah, I know.
Just ignore me. Do your thing.

397
00:25:28.250 --> 00:25:31.750
Tough! Your presence is
really affecting your art.

398
00:25:32.833 --> 00:25:34.333
You interested or should I go?

399
00:25:35.416 --> 00:25:36.708
Are you breaking up with me?

400
00:25:41.958 --> 00:25:43.166
How old are you?

401
00:25:43.250 --> 00:25:44.291
Twenty-five.

402
00:25:45.625 --> 00:25:48.625
-What do you do?
-I'm a stand-up comic.

403
00:25:48.708 --> 00:25:51.250
You know the problem with political jokes?

404
00:25:51.333 --> 00:25:52.833
They get elected sometimes.

405
00:25:53.958 --> 00:25:54.833
Why comedy?

406
00:25:56.166 --> 00:25:57.250
Dad, is that you?

407
00:25:58.875 --> 00:26:01.833
When did you first realize you were funny?

408
00:26:03.416 --> 00:26:06.291
I think it was when I was really sad.

409
00:26:12.625 --> 00:26:14.166
What's with this ring?

410
00:26:17.708 --> 00:26:18.958
It belonged to my mother.

411
00:26:24.583 --> 00:26:25.833
You ever been in love?

412
00:26:28.875 --> 00:26:31.666
What? Come on,
never had your heart broken?

413
00:26:32.750 --> 00:26:33.750
Once.

414
00:26:34.416 --> 00:26:35.708
How old were you?

415
00:26:38.625 --> 00:26:40.208
-Nine.
-Nine?

416
00:26:41.708 --> 00:26:43.125
We don't get to choose that shit.

417
00:26:50.541 --> 00:26:53.625
"So, have you ever been in love?"

418
00:26:59.250 --> 00:27:01.250
Yes. I have.

419
00:27:06.958 --> 00:27:08.000
Bye, Zeeshan.

420
00:27:10.291 --> 00:27:11.875
It's Imaad.

421
00:27:11.958 --> 00:27:15.583
-What?
-Zeeshan's for Tinder. My name is Imaad.

422
00:27:16.208 --> 00:27:17.208
Wow!

423
00:27:18.083 --> 00:27:18.958
Bye.

424
00:27:33.708 --> 00:27:38.250
The easiest way to change one's
perspective is to move to a new city.

425
00:27:39.875 --> 00:27:42.416
Life is a collection of moments.

426
00:27:43.875 --> 00:27:45.416
Choose your lens wisely.

427
00:27:55.833 --> 00:27:57.875
C'mon, Ashish, let's go, brother.
No stopping.

428
00:27:57.958 --> 00:27:59.333
Squat deeper. Engage the core.

429
00:27:59.416 --> 00:28:03.291
Less of shoulders. C'mon, engage the core.
Keep going. No stopping. Use--

430
00:28:04.750 --> 00:28:06.875
-Take it easy.
-Dude.

431
00:28:08.333 --> 00:28:11.041
-Yeezy 350s?
-Yeah, bro.

432
00:28:11.125 --> 00:28:13.250
Been trying to cop these babies
for months.

433
00:28:14.333 --> 00:28:16.625
-All right! 30 seconds up. C'mon.
-Bro.

434
00:28:17.541 --> 00:28:18.875
You're gonna kill me, bro.

435
00:28:19.791 --> 00:28:21.833
That's why I tell you
to come to the gym.

436
00:28:21.916 --> 00:28:24.125
You'll feel more motivated
seeing other people.

437
00:28:24.208 --> 00:28:26.333
Too crowded, man. Not my scene.

438
00:28:28.333 --> 00:28:31.500
Wait till I open my own studio.
It'll be perfect for you.

439
00:28:33.750 --> 00:28:35.791
-You're opening your own studio?
-Yeah.

440
00:28:35.875 --> 00:28:38.833
Only ten clients at a time.
Tailor-made services for each.

441
00:28:38.916 --> 00:28:42.083
Calisthenics, CrossFit, power lifting,
yoga, you name it.

442
00:28:42.666 --> 00:28:45.333
Superb, bro. Sign me up, baby.

443
00:28:46.041 --> 00:28:47.375
All right. Let's get this.

444
00:28:48.083 --> 00:28:49.791
Squat. That's it!

445
00:28:49.875 --> 00:28:51.333
I did a market survey.

446
00:28:51.416 --> 00:28:53.958
The fitness industry is booming.
You have to do it.

447
00:28:54.041 --> 00:28:56.875
-I'm preparing a budget.
-You need a business plan.

448
00:28:56.958 --> 00:28:59.583
If only ten clients come at a time,
how will you make money?

449
00:29:01.208 --> 00:29:04.041
Your gym should be so exclusive
so that you can charge more.

450
00:29:04.125 --> 00:29:06.375
Investors must believe
this idea is scalable.

451
00:29:06.875 --> 00:29:08.041
Yeah.

452
00:29:08.125 --> 00:29:11.208
You know what I think?
There should be two studios in Mumbai.

453
00:29:11.291 --> 00:29:14.875
-One in Bangalore, one in Delhi.
-Dude, that is the dream.

454
00:29:15.458 --> 00:29:18.666
And you can launch an app.
You can have a nutritionist.

455
00:29:18.750 --> 00:29:22.791
You can have specialized meals,
athleisure, diet plans.

456
00:29:22.875 --> 00:29:24.833
You can have kickboxing, Zumba.

457
00:29:24.916 --> 00:29:26.166
-Shit.
-Everything.

458
00:29:27.583 --> 00:29:28.666
What?

459
00:29:29.791 --> 00:29:31.250
MBA, bitches!

460
00:29:35.250 --> 00:29:38.541
If I found someone like you,
I'd be sorted.

461
00:29:40.333 --> 00:29:42.791
Why "like" me? You've got me.

462
00:29:44.875 --> 00:29:45.750
What about your job?

463
00:29:47.291 --> 00:29:48.125
I'll quit.

464
00:29:49.250 --> 00:29:51.000
That place is a dead end.

465
00:29:52.708 --> 00:29:54.916
You'll run everything.
You set up the studio,

466
00:29:55.000 --> 00:29:57.041
I'll handle expansion and management.

467
00:30:00.458 --> 00:30:03.458
-You're hired. Let's do this.
-Seriously?

468
00:30:03.541 --> 00:30:04.666
You're hired!

469
00:30:05.833 --> 00:30:06.708
What about the money?

470
00:30:06.791 --> 00:30:09.791
We'll make a killer pitch,
flirt with some investors.

471
00:30:11.125 --> 00:30:12.083
Guys.

472
00:30:12.583 --> 00:30:13.583
I'm in.

473
00:30:15.041 --> 00:30:16.625
How much money do you need?

474
00:30:18.166 --> 00:30:19.166
How?

475
00:30:20.791 --> 00:30:24.583
Mum left me some money,
and I have to invest it smartly.

476
00:30:24.666 --> 00:30:27.250
This is how.

477
00:30:28.375 --> 00:30:30.458
-Bro, you're serious?
-Yeah.

478
00:30:30.541 --> 00:30:33.000
Imaad, we humbly accept your offer.

479
00:30:33.833 --> 00:30:37.333
But, guys, it'll take time to break even,
so you must be sure.

480
00:30:38.708 --> 00:30:42.500
Look, guys. If I have to invest,
I want to invest in you two.

481
00:30:42.583 --> 00:30:43.583
I trust you guys.

482
00:30:44.166 --> 00:30:46.875
Fuck! Guys, is this actually happening?

483
00:30:47.458 --> 00:30:48.500
It is.

484
00:30:49.250 --> 00:30:51.500
Shit!

485
00:30:53.750 --> 00:30:56.083
-To the Jungle Gym.
-The Jungle Gym?

486
00:30:56.708 --> 00:30:59.583
-The Jungle Gym.
-I love it.

487
00:30:59.666 --> 00:31:01.250
To the Jungle Gym!

488
00:31:01.333 --> 00:31:04.625
So, friends, let us convert our friendship
into a relationship!

489
00:31:08.541 --> 00:31:10.250
To the Jungle Gym!

490
00:31:25.625 --> 00:31:27.958
I wanna see you dance

491
00:31:33.416 --> 00:31:35.583
I wanna see you dance

492
00:31:35.666 --> 00:31:37.750
-Sir, your bill.
-Give it here.

493
00:31:38.708 --> 00:31:40.583
-You always pay.
-Chill, man.

494
00:31:41.291 --> 00:31:42.958
Is this what boys like?

495
00:31:44.291 --> 00:31:47.000
-Let it go! Why you looking at her?
-I've made a fake account.

496
00:31:47.083 --> 00:31:48.000
What?

497
00:31:48.500 --> 00:31:51.458
Or else she'll know
I'm following her stories.

498
00:31:51.541 --> 00:31:54.291
Just ask Rohan.
Why are you playing detective?

499
00:31:54.791 --> 00:31:57.500
She needs to block Rohan. And drink.

500
00:31:58.583 --> 00:31:59.458
Fine.

501
00:32:00.333 --> 00:32:02.208
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

502
00:32:03.375 --> 00:32:04.500
Isn't that Lala?

503
00:32:06.041 --> 00:32:07.000
