01:50:47.416 --> 01:50:48.708
Let me think.

1517
01:50:48.791 --> 01:50:51.833
You slept with me and then you blocked me.

1518
01:50:52.375 --> 01:50:55.708
And then you went for waffles with "baby."
Maybe that's why, Rohan.

1519
01:50:56.875 --> 01:50:57.958
Why can't I speak?

1520
01:51:01.541 --> 01:51:03.583
-Imaad.
-Hey, Aisha. What's up?

1521
01:51:04.291 --> 01:51:06.625
-You could've called.
-You blocked me.

1522
01:51:07.583 --> 01:51:11.958
-Ahana, can we speak tomorrow, please?
-Why did you hook up with me?

1523
01:51:14.458 --> 01:51:15.750
You don't know.

1524
01:51:15.833 --> 01:51:17.500
Maybe your friends know…

1525
01:51:17.583 --> 01:51:21.041
No. I just wanted closure. Okay?

1526
01:51:21.125 --> 01:51:25.125
-Things ended so abruptly.
-Abruptly?

1527
01:51:25.250 --> 01:51:26.750
You ended it, you piece of shit.

1528
01:51:26.833 --> 01:51:30.208
But we didn't get a chance
to say a proper goodbye.

1529
01:51:30.291 --> 01:51:33.833
Because you lied!
You said you wanted a break.

1530
01:51:33.916 --> 01:51:35.500
Is this your way of saying goodbye?

1531
01:51:35.583 --> 01:51:37.583
Is that why you were texting me, Rohan?

1532
01:51:38.166 --> 01:51:40.708
I just want us to be friends. Okay?

1533
01:51:40.791 --> 01:51:42.833
Is that how you talk to your friends?

1534
01:51:42.916 --> 01:51:44.708
"Hi, baby, you look so hot."

1535
01:51:45.291 --> 01:51:46.125
Rohan?

1536
01:51:46.208 --> 01:51:47.833
I was complimenting you, okay?

1537
01:51:47.916 --> 01:51:50.750
-If you got offended, not my problem.
-I wasn't offended.

1538
01:51:50.833 --> 01:51:53.666
You flirted with me, and I flirted
back and we hooked up.

1539
01:51:54.333 --> 01:51:57.416
I'm sorry. I feel like shit about it.

1540
01:51:58.708 --> 01:52:00.083
You feel like shit?

1541
01:52:00.166 --> 01:52:02.750
I feel like shit since we broke up.
But do you care?

1542
01:52:02.833 --> 01:52:04.333
Sure, I care, but you seemed happy.

1543
01:52:04.416 --> 01:52:06.833
-When?
-I saw your posts.

1544
01:52:06.916 --> 01:52:08.083
You even went on a date.

1545
01:52:09.250 --> 01:52:11.666
You have moved on. Just admit it.

1546
01:52:11.750 --> 01:52:14.083
It wasn't a date. I was just pretending.

1547
01:52:15.291 --> 01:52:18.791
Seeing your super happy life
and your perfect girlfriend everyday,

1548
01:52:18.916 --> 01:52:20.083
I'm fed up, Rohan.

1549
01:52:20.166 --> 01:52:21.833
Then stop looking. Why are you looking?

1550
01:52:21.916 --> 01:52:25.333
I don't know. I can't stop.

1551
01:52:27.791 --> 01:52:30.041
I just wanted your attention, Rohan.

1552
01:52:35.916 --> 01:52:37.083
Wow.

1553
01:52:43.833 --> 01:52:45.166
I'm so stupid.

1554
01:52:47.708 --> 01:52:50.708
To think my self-worth depended
on an asshole like you.

1555
01:52:56.625 --> 01:52:58.708
Ask him where he was on the sangeet night.

1556
01:52:59.750 --> 01:53:00.916
Ahana, what the hell?

1557
01:54:01.791 --> 01:54:02.958
Ahana!

1558
01:54:14.041 --> 01:54:14.875
It's okay.

1559
01:54:16.750 --> 01:54:17.750
Let's go home.

1560
01:54:18.416 --> 01:54:19.791
No.

1561
01:54:22.083 --> 01:54:22.916
Fuck!

1562
01:54:25.958 --> 01:54:27.541
That was a bitch move, Ahana.

1563
01:54:29.166 --> 01:54:30.000
Imaad.

1564
01:54:30.500 --> 01:54:31.625
Is that how you talk?

1565
01:54:32.125 --> 01:54:33.458
What you gonna do?

1566
01:54:34.375 --> 01:54:37.083
Imaad, leave it, please. Stop it, guys.

1567
01:54:37.166 --> 01:54:38.500
-Stay out of it.
-Stay out?

1568
01:54:38.583 --> 01:54:40.250
-What are you doing, Rohan?
-No touching!

1569
01:54:40.333 --> 01:54:42.708
-Stay out of it.
-Imaad, what are you doing?

1570
01:54:42.791 --> 01:54:45.333
Guys, stop it! What are you doing?

1571
01:54:45.416 --> 01:54:47.125
Imaad, stop it!

1572
01:54:48.375 --> 01:54:49.708
Rohan, get off him!

1573
01:54:50.291 --> 01:54:52.083
Rohan, stop it. You're hurting him.

1574
01:55:15.000 --> 01:55:17.000
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

1575
01:55:17.083 --> 01:55:19.375
You broke my nose.
Now see what I do to you.

1576
01:55:20.250 --> 01:55:21.666
That was a bitch move, Neil.

1577
01:55:24.833 --> 01:55:25.958
Let's get out of here.

1578
01:55:29.666 --> 01:55:32.500
You're something. Good timing.

1579
01:55:32.583 --> 01:55:34.625
He deserved a few birthday bumps.

1580
01:55:35.708 --> 01:55:37.583
You should've given one more from me.

1581
01:55:48.458 --> 01:55:49.625
Neil.

1582
01:55:50.583 --> 01:55:52.125
Have you seen Lala's page?

1583
01:55:52.875 --> 01:55:53.916
What happened?

1584
01:55:55.041 --> 01:55:57.291
Look at her page. She's getting bullied.

1585
01:55:59.083 --> 01:56:00.291
Look at the comments.

1586
01:56:00.375 --> 01:56:04.500
She's photoshopped her images.
Apparently, she's done her lips.

1587
01:56:05.083 --> 01:56:07.625
-Shit!
-Obviously she's been hacked.

1588
01:56:07.708 --> 01:56:08.958
Who'd do such a thing?

1589
01:56:09.458 --> 01:56:11.750
-Now they're all trolling her.
-Look at this.

1590
01:56:12.750 --> 01:56:16.250
"Lightened skin, social climber, sellout."

1591
01:56:16.333 --> 01:56:17.708
This is horrible, dude.

1592
01:56:17.833 --> 01:56:19.166
-I know.
-"Nose job."

1593
01:56:20.333 --> 01:56:22.416
"A Nagpur call center accent."

1594
01:56:25.916 --> 01:56:27.500
Neil, call her.

1595
01:56:28.250 --> 01:56:30.958
She should file a complaint.
This is messed up.

1596
01:56:33.916 --> 01:56:34.958
Neil?

1597
01:56:38.166 --> 01:56:39.000
What is it?

1598
01:56:43.500 --> 01:56:44.708
I hacked her account.

1599
01:56:46.708 --> 01:56:47.625
What?

1600
01:56:49.416 --> 01:56:52.375
-I put up that first post.
-Why?

1601
01:57:00.000 --> 01:57:01.916
She complained about me to Harsh.

1602
01:57:02.500 --> 01:57:03.791
I was fired from the gym.

1603
01:57:05.416 --> 01:57:06.541
You guys broke up?

1604
01:57:07.875 --> 01:57:09.500
She cheated on me.

1605
01:57:12.250 --> 01:57:15.625
I didn't have what she was looking for,
so she found someone else.

1606
01:57:17.833 --> 01:57:19.958
She put up a story,
kissing that guy while I was--

1607
01:57:20.083 --> 01:57:22.375
Neil, I'm sorry that you were hurt,

1608
01:57:22.958 --> 01:57:24.708
but that doesn't mean you take revenge.

1609
01:57:25.916 --> 01:57:27.958
I can't believe you would do this, Neil.

1610
01:57:51.916 --> 01:57:53.208
What you are and have…

1611
01:57:55.291 --> 01:57:57.291
maybe she couldn't see it.

1612
01:57:59.083 --> 01:58:00.291
And neither can you.

1613
01:58:00.958 --> 01:58:02.708
That's the problem.

1614
01:58:11.333 --> 01:58:12.333
Yeah.

1615
01:58:58.250 --> 01:59:01.541
"Lala, I hacked
into your account yesterday."

1616
01:59:02.958 --> 01:59:04.666
"I put up that post in your name."

1617
01:59:05.875 --> 01:59:07.291
"I violated your privacy."

1618
01:59:09.291 --> 01:59:11.041
"I wanted to humiliate you."

1619
01:59:11.125 --> 01:59:12.583
"I just wanted to shame you."

1620
01:59:13.541 --> 01:59:15.375
"But what happened since

1621
01:59:16.041 --> 01:59:17.708
"has left me ashamed of myself."

1622
01:59:18.833 --> 01:59:22.291
"I don't have an explanation
for my actions."

1623
01:59:24.375 --> 01:59:27.125
"Except that I wasn't happy with myself."

1624
01:59:29.333 --> 01:59:31.416
"All I saw were my shortcomings."

1625
01:59:32.541 --> 01:59:35.250
"I was so caught up
with what I don't have,

1626
01:59:35.875 --> 01:59:41.291
"that I never saw or appreciated
the things I have."

1627
01:59:47.375 --> 01:59:49.041
"I had forgotten to be grateful."

1628
01:59:51.750 --> 01:59:55.333
"I don't expect to be forgiven, Lala.
I crossed a line."

1629
01:59:55.416 --> 01:59:58.500
"And I'm ready to face the consequences."

1630
02:00:01.500 --> 02:00:05.375
"But I want you and everyone else to know

1631
02:00:05.458 --> 02:00:08.666
"that the things I wrote show my reality."

1632
02:00:09.625 --> 02:00:10.583
"Not yours."

1633
02:00:11.375 --> 02:00:13.333
"I'm truly sorry to have hurt you, Lala."

1634
02:00:14.041 --> 02:00:15.166
"Neil Pereira."

1635
02:00:20.875 --> 02:00:25.750
Dating apps should've made life easier,
but meeting someone is even tougher.

1636
02:00:25.833 --> 02:00:29.125
The thing is, now we reject people
at a superficial level.

1637
02:00:29.750 --> 02:00:32.250
"I don't want to date
somebody named Jignesh."

1638
02:00:33.000 --> 02:00:36.041
She's an investment banker?
No, she'll keep repeating,

1639
02:00:36.125 --> 02:00:38.291
"Mutual fund investments are
subject to market risks."

1640
02:00:38.375 --> 02:00:41.375
"Please read the offer document carefully
before committing."

1641
02:00:43.083 --> 02:00:45.750
In this world of easy judgements
and shallow connections,

1642
02:00:45.833 --> 02:00:47.541
I finally managed to find someone.

1643
02:00:48.041 --> 02:00:51.416
Somebody I could trust,
maybe fall in love with.

1644
02:00:52.875 --> 02:00:53.708
Thank you.

1645
02:00:53.791 --> 02:00:56.500
And in classic Imaad style,
I completely screwed it up.

1646
02:00:57.083 --> 02:01:00.875
For the first time it felt good.
I was comfortable with someone.

1647
02:01:00.958 --> 02:01:02.291
Then a voice from my heart said,

1648
02:01:02.375 --> 02:01:05.250
"Man, it's been a while
since I enjoyed an Arijit Singh song."

1649
02:01:06.833 --> 02:01:11.500
Seriously, the person I've had the longest
and most consistent relationship with

1650
02:01:11.583 --> 02:01:12.750
is my therapist.

1651
02:01:14.875 --> 02:01:16.416
My therapist asked me,

1652
02:01:16.500 --> 02:01:19.958
"Imaad, when was the last time
you had an intimate relationship?"

1653
02:01:20.541 --> 02:01:22.916
I was like, "Last night."

1654
02:01:24.291 --> 02:01:25.625
"It was very intimate."

1655
02:01:26.750 --> 02:01:27.666
And she was like,

1656
02:01:27.750 --> 02:01:30.666
"Imaad, this is my therapy clinic,
not Koffee with Karan."

1657
02:01:32.208 --> 02:01:34.500
"I'm talking about emotional intimacy."

1658
02:01:37.083 --> 02:01:41.208
And for the first time in my life,
even as a comedian, I had no comeback.

1659
02:01:47.041 --> 02:01:48.416
Emotional intimacy.

1660
02:01:51.791 --> 02:01:54.291
I feel like if I open up to people,

1661
02:01:55.000 --> 02:01:56.375
they'll judge me and leave.

1662
02:01:57.291 --> 02:02:00.000
So, before they can leave me,
I leave them.

1663
02:02:01.166 --> 02:02:04.125
I still lose out in the end.
But you see, my ego is on a high.

1664
02:02:07.083 --> 02:02:09.291
I'm used to being alone since I was a kid.

1665
02:02:09.833 --> 02:02:11.750
I was nine when my mother passed away.

1666
02:02:11.833 --> 02:02:14.875
My dad decided he would not spend
the rest of his life alone.

1667
02:02:15.458 --> 02:02:20.375
So every evening, he'd chill with
a Mr. Johnnie Walker, or with an Old Monk.

1668
02:02:22.583 --> 02:02:26.166
This was his version of therapy.
Cheap and effective.

1669
02:02:29.000 --> 02:02:32.458
Sometimes his business partners
would come over for drinks.

1670
02:02:32.541 --> 02:02:35.041
One night dad indulged
in too much therapy,

1671
02:02:35.625 --> 02:02:36.791
so he went to bed.

1672
02:02:37.833 --> 02:02:41.208
His business partner came to me,
and he offered me chocolates.

1673
02:02:42.250 --> 02:02:46.416
Now, for a ten-year-old, to get chocolates
is like winning the lottery.

1674
02:02:50.208 --> 02:02:52.041
He asked me where the washroom was.

1675
02:02:53.708 --> 02:02:54.833
I took him there.

1676
02:02:55.666 --> 02:02:58.208
And suddenly he pulled me in with him.

1677
02:03:01.000 --> 02:03:03.833
Before I could even process
what was happening to me,

1678
02:03:05.208 --> 02:03:06.708
it happened again.

1679
02:03:09.875 --> 02:03:11.041
Then again.

1680
02:03:12.666 --> 02:03:13.916
And another night.

1681
02:03:17.375 --> 02:03:18.833
And more chocolates.

1682
02:03:21.541 --> 02:03:23.625
The wrappers started piling up.

1683
02:03:29.416 --> 02:03:31.125
I know what you guys are thinking.

1684
02:03:31.833 --> 02:03:33.583
Imaad must really like chocolates.

1685
02:03:33.666 --> 02:03:35.333
He'd do anything for them.

1686
02:03:38.708 --> 02:03:42.250
When my dad saw the chocolates, he said,
"Son, these are expensive chocolates."

1687
02:03:42.333 --> 02:03:45.541
I said, "Yeah, Dad. You have no idea."

1688
02:03:47.375 --> 02:03:48.708
What could I have said?

1689
02:03:49.375 --> 02:03:52.083
Your business partner is
mixing business with pleasure?

1690
02:04:02.916 --> 02:04:05.500
What's going on, guys?
Don't be awkward, you can laugh.

1691
02:04:06.875 --> 02:04:08.875
If you don't, you'll spoil my show.

1692
02:04:09.625 --> 02:04:12.916
And I can't even eat chocolates
to cheer myself up.

1693
02:04:21.833 --> 02:04:22.958
Intimacy.

1694
02:04:23.916 --> 02:04:25.500
Into-me-see.

1695
02:04:29.375 --> 02:04:31.833
For the past fifteen years,
I've had only one aim.

1696
02:04:32.708 --> 02:04:34.375
That no one should know my truth.

1697
02:04:37.708 --> 02:04:39.125
No one should see it.

1698
02:04:39.791 --> 02:04:41.875
I snuck my way through life till here.

1699
02:04:43.041 --> 02:04:46.208
I did whatever I had to. I lied.

1700
02:04:46.791 --> 02:04:48.375
Spoiled relationships.

1701
02:04:49.083 --> 02:04:50.541
Cracked stupid jokes.

1702
02:04:51.250 --> 02:04:52.458
To avoid the truth.

1703
02:04:55.125 --> 02:04:57.791
I never even told my friends about it.

1704
02:04:59.041 --> 02:05:02.083
I thought it was my fault.

1705
02:05:04.333 --> 02:05:05.625
That night…

1706
02:05:07.833 --> 02:05:09.708
What could a ten-year-old have done?

1707
02:05:10.666 --> 02:05:12.083
He could've shouted.

1708
02:05:14.208 --> 02:05:16.333
Tried to stop it. Could've run away.

1709
02:05:19.166 --> 02:05:20.625
And since that day,

1710
02:05:22.000 --> 02:05:23.291
all I've done is run.

1711
02:05:27.875 --> 02:05:29.416
But not anymore.

1712
02:05:31.916 --> 02:05:34.291
I've spent 15 years of my life
with this shame.

1713
02:05:36.375 --> 02:05:37.500
I'm done.

1714
02:05:45.791 --> 02:05:48.333
Tonight I'm taking control of my life
back in my hands.

1715
02:05:52.208 --> 02:05:54.750
And there could be
no better place to share.

1716
02:05:55.666 --> 02:05:58.458
'Cause if I regret telling you this,
I can always say,

1717
02:05:59.291 --> 02:06:00.416
"It was a joke."

1718
02:07:17.875 --> 02:07:19.583
It's 31st of December.

1719
02:07:20.166 --> 02:07:21.458
We're a bit older.

1720
02:07:22.041 --> 02:07:23.375
And a lot wiser.

1721
02:07:24.083 --> 02:07:26.333
Wise to the fact that,
like any drug addict

1722
02:07:27.041 --> 02:07:29.166
the problem wasn't chasing the high,

1723
02:07:29.250 --> 02:07:31.000
it was running away from reality.

1724
02:07:32.291 --> 02:07:34.708
We got so lost in our screens,

1725
02:07:34.791 --> 02:07:36.791
we forgot to look within ourselves.

1726
02:07:37.416 --> 02:07:39.750
Since today is a day for new beginnings,

1727
02:07:40.458 --> 02:07:41.666
let's reboot.

1728
02:07:45.166 --> 02:07:46.125
Resolution one.

1729
02:07:48.166 --> 02:07:49.833
Put your phone down.

1730
02:07:50.583 --> 02:07:51.958
And look up.

1731
02:07:54.875 --> 02:07:56.750
Look life in the eye.

1732
02:08:00.000 --> 02:08:01.708
Because life is meant for living.

1733
02:08:02.375 --> 02:08:04.666
Without filters, without lenses.

1734
02:08:10.250 --> 02:08:11.416
Resolution two.

1735
02:08:13.000 --> 02:08:15.416
Take it easy, keep it real.

1736
02:08:16.125 --> 02:08:19.250
Recognize that it doesn't take much
to be happy.

1737
02:08:20.583 --> 02:08:22.958
Only when you truly connect with yourself

1738
02:08:23.541 --> 02:08:25.333
can people truly connect with you.

1739
02:08:26.458 --> 02:08:29.958
We're free of all our woes
That's all we know

1740
02:08:30.541 --> 02:08:34.291
We'll heed our hearts
We'll follow them where they go

1741
02:08:35.458 --> 02:08:36.583
Resolution three.

1742
02:08:36.666 --> 02:08:38.041
Stop the comparisons.

1743
02:08:38.583 --> 02:08:42.666
No one is like you,
and you don't need to be like anyone else.

1744
02:08:44.791 --> 02:08:48.583
Where did we lose ourselves?

1745
02:08:52.750 --> 02:08:56.083
Where did we lose ourselves?

1746
02:08:56.166 --> 02:08:57.250
You are unique.

1747
02:08:57.333 --> 02:09:00.000
The only person better than you today
is you tomorrow.

1748
02:09:07.708 --> 02:09:09.916
Resolution four. Be grateful.

1749
02:09:13.708 --> 02:09:18.750
Say "Thank you."
Loud and clear. Every day.

1750
02:09:20.208 --> 02:09:27.041
Why think of things
That make us feel so low?

1751
02:09:29.458 --> 02:09:33.208
We're free of all our woes
That's all we really know

1752
02:09:35.083 --> 02:09:36.375
And resolution five.

1753
02:09:36.958 --> 02:09:37.875
Find your tribe.

1754
02:09:38.666 --> 02:09:41.875
Because who needs followers
when you have friends?

1755
02:09:47.750 --> 02:09:51.125
Where did we lose ourselves?

1756
02:09:55.750 --> 02:10:01.416
Where did we lose ourselves?
